#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:3
msgid "Standalone Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:5
msgid ""
"Install an app under a Python interpreter downloaded from `python-build-"
"standalone <https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone>`_ instead "
"of the system one. Reach for this when the system Python lacks the version "
"you need, or when a distro patched its Python in ways that break the app. "
"pipx only downloads final releases: it skips alpha, beta and release "
"candidate builds, so a version with no final release yet, such as 3.16 "
"during its alphas, cannot be fetched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:13
msgid "How pipx decides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:15
msgid ""
"``--fetch-python`` (or ``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON``) sets the policy. Without ``--"
"python``, pipx first looks for a local interpreter that satisfies the app's "
"``requires-python``, and the policy only decides what happens when none does:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:38
msgid ""
"When you name ``--python`` yourself, pipx uses that interpreter and reports "
"it, rather than overriding you when the package rejects it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:43
msgid "Set the policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:49
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:50
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:51
msgid "``never``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:52
msgid ""
"Default. Never download; use interpreters from ``PATH`` or the ``py`` "
"launcher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:53
msgid "``missing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:54
msgid "Look locally first; download when the requested version is not found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:55
msgid "``always``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:56
msgid ""
"Skip the local search and use a standalone build for the version named with "
"``--python``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:58
msgid ""
"$ pipx install --python 3.13 --fetch-python=missing my-package\n"
"$ pipx install --python 3.13 --fetch-python=always my-package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:63
msgid "Set it for the whole shell session with the environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:65
msgid ""
"$ export PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON=missing\n"
"$ pipx install --python 3.13 my-package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:70
msgid ""
"Reach for ``always`` in CI runs that should not depend on the runner's "
"Python, on distros that strip modules like ``tkinter`` or ``lzma``, or on "
"air-gapped hosts with a populated standalone cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:75
msgid "Manage cached interpreters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:77
msgid ""
"pipx unpacks each interpreter into its standalone cache. Manage them with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:79
msgid ""
"$ pipx interpreter list\n"
"$ pipx interpreter prune\n"
"$ pipx interpreter upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:85
msgid ""
"``interpreter upgrade`` moves environments on standalone builds to the "
"newest patch release of their minor version, including environments "
"installed with an exact version such as ``--python 3.14.8``. If a build "
"cannot be downloaded, pipx reports the failure and continues with other "
"builds. If an environment cannot be rebuilt, pipx reports it and continues "
"with the other environments. This includes a package whose ``Requires-"
"Python`` rules out the new build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:90
msgid ""
"The command exits with an error if any upgrade fails. Use ``--output json`` "
"to read the failures alongside the completed environment upgrades. Rerun the "
"command after resolving a failure to finish rebuilding affected environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:95
msgid ""
"``--fetch-missing-python`` and ``PIPX_FETCH_MISSING_PYTHON`` still work but "
"are deprecated aliases for ``--fetch-python=missing`` / "
"``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON=missing``. pipx errors if you set both "
"``PIPX_FETCH_MISSING_PYTHON`` and ``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:101
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:103
msgid "$ pipx list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/standalone-python.rst:107
msgid ""
"The environment lists the interpreter version pipx settled on. For how pipx "
"resolves interpreters, see :doc:`../explanation/how-pipx-works`."
msgstr ""
